{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 34.8% a year from $404.5 million in FY2016 to $5.93 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F196]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was a step change, not a smooth compound: growth of 64.2% in FY2021 [D218] collapsed to 11.8% in FY2022 [D263] and 0.1% in FY2023 [D311], then recovered to 16.4% in FY2024 [D358] and 10.6% in FY2025 [D406]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2017 loss of $3.45 billion [F32] was driven by a $2.6 billion increase in stock-based compensation, primarily the CEO award and RSUs tied to the IPO [P74]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin has improved every year since FY2017's -422.5% [F22], reaching -9.0% in FY2025 [F30], a 5.7pp gain on FY2024 [D419]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2025 revenue rose $570.0 million, with advertising up $282.4 million on roughly 17% more impressions and other revenue up $287.6 million on subscriber growth [P24]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Other revenue contributed 5.4pp of the 10.6% growth and reached 12.6% of revenue in FY2025, up from 4.3% in FY2023 [D545][D543][D539]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "North America remains the largest geography at 58.6% of revenue but contributed only 4.4pp of FY2025 growth, against 3.7pp from Rest of world [D456][D458][D499]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 5.1pp slower than revenue in FY2025 [D430], at 5.1% [D423], and the incremental operating margin was 44.8% [D429]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted shares rose 2.1% in FY2025 [D425], so the 35.7% smaller EPS loss [D410] outpaced the 34.0% smaller net loss [D408]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "FY2025 operating margin of -9.0% [F30] sits above the -32.4% window median [D555] and is the window high [D554]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The 5.7pp FY2025 improvement [D419] came from cost of revenue (+1.1pp) [D431], R&D (+1.3pp) [D432] and other lines (+3.3pp) [D433]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Sales and marketing fell $42.4 million on the timing of marketing events and lower advertising, partly offset by higher headcount [P22], while R&D rose $101.9 million on product development headcount [P23]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of -7.8% [F50] sat 1.2pp above the -9.0% operating margin [F30], helped by $68.9 million of other income [X130] that included $96.7 million of debt-extinguishment gains [P18]."}
